# Build-context exclusions for Podman image builds from `backend/`
# (used by reader/Containerfile; Podman reads .containerignore).
#
# The first block is load-bearing for security: reader/Containerfile does
# `COPY reader ./reader`, which would otherwise bake a developer's local
# reader/.env — real keyset material and database URL — into the image.
#
# Root-relative patterns (.env, .env.*) only match at the build-context root
# (backend/), NOT backend/reader/.env — verified empirically: without the
# **/ variants below, `podman build` + `podman export` shows reader/.env
# present in the image. The **/ patterns match at any depth and are the
# ones actually doing the exclusion; the root patterns are kept for the
# (unlikely) case of a stray backend/.env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# Not needed at runtime; keeps the image small and the context clean.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
dist/
build/
*.log
